2924b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104446" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $2\\pi $ | $-3$ | $\\pi $ | $5$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=4.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))=f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=4} & =f(4){g}^{′}(4)+g(4){f}^{′}(4) \\\\  & =2\\pi \\cdot 5+(-3)\\cdot \\pi  \\\\  & =7\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104446/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104446"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48836/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "ea7ddc8c-65aa-5b9d-bc7f-93a35d7d755e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48836/selection/e4feab3a7179f2a87633c6e7922d72261df298535ed5bf9932c62a0940c0196c" :answer/id #uuid "76657296-d86a-516f-a1b1-b074c29c7ae6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48836/selection/b01ba7e917b2f2dc3ff90ccb2c435764c9ebef2dea263cc318e0c231eb7eeb1d" :answer/id #uuid "f479f571-8f10-566f-ba16-4b3304d706d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48836/selection/17f7a92ecac965d3850a7da98658af322c6b691d4b3336f622586133c927298d" :answer/id #uuid "efaf69f4-fd40-59e3-a2e5-379a571bb8c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} 