q-48836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340503/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "203541fa-b636-50ed-90c6-522d061eced1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340503/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d670838d-0d21-5c8e-9f04-3376e3fec080" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340503/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-340503/field-1/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340503" :question/id #uuid "1aecccaa-d707-522a-89aa-5451ef41462f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340503" :question/is-example false :question/problem "For the function $f(x)$ and $g(x)$, you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=-1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=3,\\,g(2)=2,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=-3\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))$ at $x=2.$ \n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the product rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x)) & =f(x){g}^{′}(x)+g(x){f}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=2} & =f(2){g}^{′}(2)+g(2){f}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-3)+2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-340503/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f08b8fa-6f05-5c10-b2d7-5d35e6c48e74"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340503"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-311277/field-1/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer/id #uuid "56797035-1680-5d16-8701-3d64a8a8a167" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-311277/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0130917-fd95-54ff-bf3a-a2a4e772d49c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-311277/field-1/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc" :answer-field/choices ["q-311277/field-1/35f5572ccca3a8c38d3ca06e2a92b51065f48e45d29833e19f4eb153cae096fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-311277" :question/id #uuid "32825630-48b0-5a25-9c00-09e9b47eedf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-311277" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=5$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5$ | $3$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $6$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=5.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=5}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=5$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=5} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(5)g(5)-f(5){g}^{′}(5)}{(g(5))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)(-2)-(3)(6)}{(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-18}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{10}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-311277/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-311277"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48844"] :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=0} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(0)g(0)-f(0){g}^{′}(0)}{{g}^{2}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-341013/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "ed7bb281-eb41-5aa3-9e1c-28289c935272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341013/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "34ba2c5e-4ef9-565d-8f81-e9803ccf4665" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341013/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-341013/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341013" :question/id #uuid "0a336c52-99c0-50c9-8e2c-de3211889702" :question/math-academy-id "q-341013" :question/is-example false :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,g(4)=\\sqrt{2},\\,{g}^{′}(4)=-1\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=4.$\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=4} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(4)g(4)-f(4){g}^{′}(4)}{(g(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}-2\\cdot (-1)}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+2}{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341013/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowled