8b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48960" :question/id #uuid "71d7b6ec-4bf0-538b-a83d-e6257da5291e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48960" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=3$ are given in the table below. \n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-4$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=3$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=3} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(3)g(3)-f(3){g}^{′}(3)}{(g(3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-4)\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48960/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2b7d79a-cd1a-583f-be7a-d568bc8e32a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48960"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105324/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "f380171e-1679-5bde-8a45-17b12afafd56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105324/selection/8642f29c07ed588847b818ca52d7d9b13f60105c8ca35b3f5cb1a649a54ead1c" :answer/id #uuid "c9175c1f-fee8-50d3-a133-f7bec4f1ffd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105324/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "d70e4727-8828-51d0-a69e-4a9d9c7a81ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105324/selection/d971375f57c56