 [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104769" :question/id #uuid "a79366df-e0b9-5d49-bb7e-5065998cbac9" :question/math-academy-id "q-104769" :question/is-example false :question/problem "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(4)=-2,\\,{f}^{′}(4)=4,\\,g(4)=1,\\,{g}^{′}(4)=0\n$$\n\nIf $h(x)=\\frac{2-3f(x)}{g(x)+1},$ compute ${h}^{′}(4).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2-3f(x)$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3{f}^{′}(x)\\cdot (g(x)+1)-(2-3f(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x)}{{(g(x)+1)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{-3{f}^{′}(4)\\cdot (g(4)+1)-(2-3f(4))\\cdot {g}^{′}(4)}{{(g(4)+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 4\\cdot (1+1)-(2-3\\cdot (-2))\\cdot 0}{{(1+1)}^{2}} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-104769/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104769"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341468/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "45e83aa3-b347-5ffd-80d1-8e6e2462fd1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341468/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3" :answer/id #uuid "91521d9c-083c-55f6-b869-ac47f3f2247c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341468/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "c4759c2a-ca11-5e5b-99b4-53cd13ae80f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341468/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer-field/choices ["q-341468/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-341468/field-1/cedce138738816f1e959edfd5049bf0c6bcf0acc69b898c7f84479cb3a782ce3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341468" :question/id #uuid "d2e24374-6397-50d9-a912-6aa8e5601652" :question/math-academy-id "q-341468" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $h(t)$ and $z(t)$ and their derivatives at $t=4$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $1$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{2h(t)-5}{1-z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(4).$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}^{′}(4)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2h(t)-5$ and $v=1-z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}=-{z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2{h}^{′}(t)(1-z(t))-(2h(t)-5)(-{z}^{′}(t))}{(1-z(t))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt $t=4,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2{h}^{′}(4)(1-z(4))-(2h(4)-5)(-{z}^{′}(4))}{(1-z(4))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(1-(-2))-(2(1)-5)(-1)}{(1-(-2))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(3)(3)-(-3)(-1)}{(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{18-3}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-341468/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341468"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-341450/field-1/9514742e7e29eb2169eae9fd96756490f5d7185f306031e9167859d20cd4a484" :answer/id #uuid "755461d9-f3d2-50af-8f70-80ff462b7a0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-47" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341450/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac967da9-243d-53c7-a4d2-b97480f2d0f9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-341450/field-1/9514742e7e29eb2169eae9fd96756490f5d7185f306031e9167859d20cd4a484" :answer-field/choices ["q-341450/field-1/9514742e7e29eb2169eae9fd96756490f5d7185f306031e9167859d20cd4a484"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341450" :question/id #uuid "df7e57ca-bb3e-5704-847f-e348f6da28af" :question/math-academy-id "q-341450" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ and their derivatives at $x=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ | ${g}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $4$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n\nIf $h(x)=(-2f(x)-3)(g(x)+1),$ find the value of ${h}^{′}(2).$\n\n${h}^{′}(2)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Explanation:\n\nThe product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-2f(x)-3$ and $v=g(x)+1.$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-2{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={g}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(x) & =-2{f}^{′}(x)(g(x)+1)+(-2f(x)-3){g}^{′}(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =-2{f}^{′}(2)(g(2)+1)+(-2f(2)-3){g}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =-2(2)(-3+1)+(-2(4)-3)(5) \\\\  & =-4(-2)+(-8-3)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =8+(-11)(5) \\\\  & =8-55 \\\\  & =-47.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-341450/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341450"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "2196d4ed-be9a-5cb7-a0ba-bf90332869b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "715b4eb6-448a-5bb9-bdf2-2a18a2e27350" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "5a5ed316-0f27-57c2-ae30-9a86e0bbcb6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "9bf5760d-72c2-5cc2-b7fb-8b75c17a9d36" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "9e5685bb-de5e-5e14-bc0a-2f65cf92737c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "48fb734f-f5b3-5cbe-9a3b-da55d207dddf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105495/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer-field/choices ["q-105495/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-105495/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" "q-105495/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-105495/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-105495/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105495" :question/id #uuid "6d8ae87b-0556-525c-9089-eacb2f84dc18" :question/math-academy-id "q-105495" :question/is-example false :question/problem "For the functions $p(x)$ and $q(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\np(10)=-1,\\,{p}^{′}(10)=-2,\\,q(10)=2,\\,{q}^{′}(10)=1\n$$\n\nIf $z(x)=(2p(x)+q(x))(2-p(x))$, compute ${z}^{′}(10).$" :question/worked-solution "The product rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(uv)=u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=2p(x)+q(x)$ and $v=2-p(x).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=-{p}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the product rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(x) & =u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =(2p(x)+q(x))(-{p}^{′}(x))+(2-p(x))(2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x)) \\\\  & =-{p}^{′}(x)(2p(x)+q(x))+(2{p}^{′}(x)+{q}^{′}(x))(2-p(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $x=10,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{′}(10) & =-{p}^{′}(10)(2p(10)+q(10))+(2{p}^{′}(10)+{q}^{′}(10))(2-p(10)) \\\\  & =-(-2)(2(-1)+2)+(2(-2)+1)(2-(-1)) \\\\  & =2(-2+2)-3(2+1) \\\\  & =0-9 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105495/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105495"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "02ce33fe-47ed-5c28-8b10-a4965a425ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection/41a74576debbd77023c8544bb1312a27faaff8cd498a0748fed1b5615823e294" :answer/id #uuid "fda7ea7f-81c3-5703-9be0-b95fd1af806c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "606316ba-eff2-5cc0-a352-a77a27663ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "6494c263-609b-5eab-998b-dcdf958759ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e" :answer/id #uuid "843793ad-d0d5-5f7c-aacf-6fff8d32bccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b785d613-bec6-5161-b275-e95ff69862a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4961/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer-field/choices ["q-4961/selection/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" "q-4961/selection/41a74576debbd77023c8544bb1312a27faaff8cd498a0748fed1b5615823e294" "q-4961/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" "q-4961/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-4961/selection/d278d4936eb1c69dc660a77f5f1c7b1eb5b4a4db4aee8a8ad2dc52aa3f827f2e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4961" :question/id #uuid "642e706d-880d-5e53-b334-1d3dda07b034" :question/math-academy-id "q-4961" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The values of functions $h(x)$ and $z(x)$ and their derivatives at $t=2$ are given in the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $h(t)$ | $z(t)$ | ${h}^{′}(t)$ | ${z}^{′}(t)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $8$ | $-3$ | $4$ |\n\nIf $f(t)=\\frac{1-h(t)}{z(t)},$ compute ${f}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The quotient rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{u}{v})=\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=1-h(t)$ and $v=z(t).$ Differentiating each, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=-{h}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={z}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the quotient rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}v-u{v}^{′}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-{h}^{′}(t))\\cdot z(t)-(1-h(t))\\cdot {z}^{′}(t)}{(z(t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-z(t){h}^{′}(t)-{z}^{′}(t)(1-h(t))}{{z}^{2}(t)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $t=2,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{-z(2){h}^{′}(2)-{z}^{′}(2)(1-h(2))}{{z}^{2}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\cdot (-3)-4\\cdot (1-5)}{{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24+16}{64} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-4961/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1d07a6d-3994-5620-a756-ee6e2c0a8de6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
